#!/bin/bash
# Repo commit-msg guard. Installed into .git/hooks by .cursor/install.sh; on
# Cloud Agents it runs via Cursor's hook dispatcher (which chains to
# /workspace/.git/hooks) before the managed hooks for this phase.
#
# It (a) neutralizes Cursor's managed "Co-authored-by:" appender for this
# commit, (b) strips any Co-authored-by: trailer already in the message, and
# (c) removes a trailing period from the subject line.
set -euo pipefail

MSG_FILE="$1"

# (a) Disable the managed co-author appender before the dispatcher reaches it.
#     This hook runs first (as the repo's original commit-msg hook); dropping
#     the execute bit makes the dispatcher skip *.co-author in the same commit.
hooks_dir="$(git config core.hooksPath 2>/dev/null || true)"
if [ -n "${hooks_dir:-}" ] && [ -d "$hooks_dir" ]; then
  find "$hooks_dir" -maxdepth 1 -name '*.co-author' -exec chmod -x {} + 2>/dev/null || true
fi

# (b) Drop any Co-authored-by: trailer lines, and (c) strip a trailing period
#     from the subject (first non-blank line). Body prose is left untouched.
tmp="$(mktemp)"
awk '
  tolower($0) ~ /^[[:space:]]*co-authored-by:/ { next }
  {
    if (!subject_done && $0 ~ /[^[:space:]]/) {
      sub(/[[:space:]]*\.+[[:space:]]*$/, "", $0)
      subject_done = 1
    }
    print
  }
' "$MSG_FILE" > "$tmp" && mv "$tmp" "$MSG_FILE"

exit 0
